<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov copper imports up 13.2 pct yr/yr. [CORRECTED 05:42 GMT 27/12]</title>
<headline>Japan Nov copper imports up 13.2 pct yr/yr. [CORRECTED 05:42 GMT 27/12]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined copper imports in November rose to 29,354 tonnes, up 13.2 percent from 25,939 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Thursday.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    Nov 96	  Oct 96	  Nov 95</p>
<p> Total	    29,354	  30,267	  25,939</p>
<p>(Corrects Oct 96 figure from 130,557)</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Chile	    12,238	   8,789	   9,392</p>
<p> U.S.		3,772	   5,169	   4,353</p>
<p> Zambia	    1,836	   4,932	   3,738</p>
<p>Imports in the first 11 months of 1996 were 331,084 tonnes, down 8.7 percent (corrects figures) from 362,468 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
